ArchiveEntry "SMIB loss of synchronism (Pm>K): frequency runs away"

/*
 * Single machine, NO damping (D=0), mechanical power exceeds the maximum
 * synchronizing power: Pm > K. Then sin(delta)=Pm/K has NO solution, so
 * there is no equilibrium. The frequency grows without bound (loss of
 * synchronism). Exact nonlinear, large-signal.
 *
 *   omega' = Pm - K*sin(delta) >= Pm - K > 0.
 * Invariant: omega - (Pm-K)*t is non-decreasing, since
 *   d/dt[omega-(Pm-K)t] = omega' - (Pm-K) = K(1-sin delta) >= 0.
 * Hence omega(t) >= omega0 + (Pm-K)*t -> +infinity.
 */
ProgramVariables Real delta; Real w; Real s; Real c; Real t; Real w0; End.
Problem
  \forall K \forall Pm (
    K > 0 & Pm > K & s^2+c^2=1 & t=0 & w=w0
    ->
    [{delta'=w, w'=Pm-K*s, s'=c*w, c'=-s*w, t'=1 & s^2+c^2=1}]
    w >= w0 + (Pm-K)*t )
End.
Tactic "Proof"
  allR(1); allR(1); implyR(1);
  dC("w - (Pm-K)*t >= w0", 1);
  <( dW(1); QE, dI(1) )
End.
End.
